    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the manual says e15 is actually a leak protection error in the base of the machine, not temperature. i tried the power cycle but it's still there. how do i actually check the sensor and how do i dry out the bottom if there is water sitting down there?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A leak protection error, E15, means the machine thinks it's flooded, so it's shutting down to prevent more damage. You'll need to carefully inspect the base, looking for any visible puddles or signs of moisture around the seals or connections. If you see water, gently use towels or a wet/dry vac to remove it, making sure to check the drain pump area thoroughly. Don't try to force anything, as you don't want to accidentally trigger a more serious flood, and you might need a professional to properly diagnose the leak source.",
      "source": "target",
